
    what is jwt :
    JWt stands for Json web token : is digital signed token use to prove the identity sucre without storing session in server
    jwt is statelss

    token made 3 steps :

    Header = algorithem + token type {"alg":"HS256","type":"json"}
    payload = data like user name, role exipry {  "sub": "khana",  "role": "USER",  "iat": 1706252345,  "exp": 1706262345 }
    signature = header + payload +secret key hash - HMACSHA256(    base64(header) + "." + base64(payload),    secret_key)

    why jwt stateless
    sever dose not save the token in DB or Session

    server only need
    secret key and token sent by client

